WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.602 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:06.272
-Everybody, it's time
once again for "Corrections,"

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:10.910
and I think all in all, we had
a -- we had a pretty good week.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.779
Some cleanup from last week.

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:16.116
We did a piece...

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:19.919
on Thursday of last week
where we talked about

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:23.622
Donald Trump once said that
the American army

00:00:23.622 --> 00:00:27.293
during the Revolutionary War
took over the airports,

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:32.965
and then we said that General --
the British General Cornwallis,

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:35.235
when he tried
to escape LaGuardia,

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:37.803
asked, "Where is
ground transportation?"

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:40.006
And people pointed out
that if you were British,

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:43.676
you would say,
"Where is ground transport?"

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.979
Now, that's true,
but here's the problem.

00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:51.517
If we had said that, someone --
invariably, one of the jackals

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.320
would have said that LaGuardia
is not called ground transport,

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.822
it's called
ground transportation.

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:59.492
This is what we call
a "Corrections" pickle,

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:06.466
and there's no path forward...
that ends in salvation.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.769
Like, they're both
bad choices for me.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.136
There's no way out for me.

00:01:11.136 --> 00:01:12.438
There is one good choice,

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:16.476
but it is for you to make,
which is just to stop.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:24.917
We talked about Kellyanne Conway
crashing an F-16

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:28.087
and landing in a parachute
on the tarmac.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:33.626
In the graphic we made,
she was dressed like a skydiver.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:37.297
A lot of people pointed out if
she was in an F-16 piloting it,

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:40.132
she'd be wearing a flight suit
and a parachute --

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:44.303
she wouldn't have prepared...
for the parachuting.

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:47.406
So we'd like
to apologize to her...

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:51.978
because we know how important
veracity...is in her life.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.312
We ask--
This is sort of a thing

00:01:53.312 --> 00:01:56.950
we crowdsourced out
to our friends in Oregon

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.317
because we've been talking a lot

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:03.022
about how many movies
they shoot in Astoria, Oregon.

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:06.526
A lot of hit films --
"The Goonies,"

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:09.929
"Kindergarten Cop,"
"The Ring Two,"

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:13.266
which I referred to
as "Ring Two,"

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:14.801
which was wrong.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.770
A lot of people said it's not
"Ring Two," it's<i> "The</i> Ring Two."

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.839
However, you go
to a Blockbuster...

00:02:20.839 --> 00:02:22.108
and ask for "Ring Two"

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.110
and they say, "We don't even
know what that is."

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.814
And that's on them, you know?

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.249
They should be helpful
at a Blockbuster,

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:32.585
and the last Blockbuster
closed in 2019.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.155
So yeah, that does work.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.291
You could have gone
to a Blockbuster

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.660
trying to rent "The Ring Two."

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.797
So, but they do have --
it turns out

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.131
there is film tourism
in Astoria.

00:02:46.131 --> 00:02:50.136
They have a film museum...

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:53.006
that is in the jail
from "Goonies"...

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:56.142
which is great,
so if you're looking for

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:58.177
fun for the whole family
and, you know,

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:00.446
Disney World
falls into the sea...

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:07.720
...head on down to the jail
from "Goonies."

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.591
We've talked a lot about how
you can't do Sloth anymore...

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:12.791
and I talked about

00:03:12.791 --> 00:03:15.594
how that's been really hard
for comedians...

00:03:15.594 --> 00:03:20.566
who have, like, huge
Sloth chunks in their act.

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.601
People said,
"I see what you did there.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:26.472
'Sloth chunks,' because
the other character...

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.173
is Chunk."

00:03:28.173 --> 00:03:31.110
That was an accident.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:35.949
I had no idea I was doing that,
which is, I think, proof...

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:40.286
dare I say, of...
just how good this is.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.824
That we're, like, on accident
doing jokes that good.

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:53.299
A lot of people told me how to
say, "Don't do Sloth," in Latin,

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.801
but it was, again,
a "Corrections" pickle.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.169
There were about eight choices.

00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:59.538
The one thing that was clear
is I should not have tried

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:01.240
to look up the Latin word
for "sloth"

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.408
because Sloth is a character,

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:06.078
so I shouldn't --
it shouldn't just be like...

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:09.415
[ Speaking Latin ]

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.750
And I guess there's

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:14.087
a lot of Latin versions
of, "Don't do Sloth,"

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:17.422
because I guess this was a
problem in the Catholic Church.

00:04:17.422 --> 00:04:21.594
A lot of priests were doing...
they were doing Sloth.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.629
Like, they were doing
their Sloth impressions,

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:25.631
and it was obviously
fairly offensive to...

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:27.699
What do you call people?

00:04:27.699 --> 00:04:29.001
It's not parishioners.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.536
What do you call people
who go to Catholic church?

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:31.737
-Parishioner.
-Parishioners.

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:32.771
Oh, that's right.

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:33.940
It's very offensive,

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.474
and so they would say
to the, you know,

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.443
they would say
to the Catholic priests, like,

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:43.149
you know, [Speaks Latin]
and then they would move them.

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:45.485
But it wouldn't stop them.
They'd still do Sloth.

00:04:47.786 --> 00:04:49.622
They'd still do Sloth.

00:04:52.424 --> 00:04:54.160
They'd say they stopped.

00:04:56.962 --> 00:05:04.736
So...I talked about -- we talked
about can one person...

00:05:04.736 --> 00:05:07.906
line up, and someone said,
"One person can't line up.

00:05:07.906 --> 00:05:10.375
You can join a line
and get in line."

00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:11.477
And then I said it's like

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:14.346
that John Don poem
"No Man Is a Line."

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:15.881
People said,
"You mean John Donne.

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:16.915
You say John Donne."

00:05:16.915 --> 00:05:20.085
John Donne wrote
"No Man Is an Island."

00:05:20.085 --> 00:05:24.256
John Don wrote
"No Man Is a Line."

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:30.630
John Don was a...
John Donne parody poet.

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:34.933
Weird John.

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:36.936
The first parody poet.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:43.776
I smoked as a horse.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.244
The other day,
I pantomimed smoking as a horse.

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.979
We've talked a lot
about smoking cockroaches,

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.780
and the "Corrections" jackals
were very helpful here

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.950
and said, you know...

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.651
a cockroach wouldn't smoke
from its mouth.

00:05:52.651 --> 00:05:54.787
It would smoke
from its spiracles,

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:57.323
I think it was, which is because
its lungs are on its side,

00:05:57.323 --> 00:05:58.957
so I thought I was safe for
the horse because I was like,

00:05:58.957 --> 00:06:00.059
"You know, horses have mouths."

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.093
Turns out a couple of things.

00:06:01.093 --> 00:06:03.062
One...people pointed out,

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.698
and I should've known better,
horses, with their hooves,

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.566
could not hold a cigarette.

00:06:07.566 --> 00:06:09.268
It would have to be two,

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:12.104
so right away, this would be --
if you're correctly pantomiming,

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:13.572
if you're taking it
seriously enough

00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:17.076
to get it right...
it would be this.

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:18.744
And then also, horses,
according to --

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:21.781
again, this is just one
solitary jackal, a lone jackal,

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:23.415
and this is
the risk of "Corrections,"

00:06:23.415 --> 00:06:26.118
which is a lone jackal
tells me something

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:28.387
and I do know follow-up.

00:06:28.387 --> 00:06:30.956
But they told me that due...

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:35.494
that horses have long,
soft palates...

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:37.429
that blocks their --
I hope I'm saying this right --

00:06:37.429 --> 00:06:40.633
epiglottis, and that a horse
would smoke through their nose.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:43.269
They breathe through their nose,
so from now on,

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:45.670
if we pantomime horses smoking
on the show,

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:46.973
it would have to be...

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.775
[ Inhales ]

00:06:49.775 --> 00:06:51.744
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.112
And so that means
we're just not gonna --

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:54.747
we're not gonna do it again

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:57.449
because that's
pretty distressing to watch.

00:06:57.449 --> 00:07:00.719
A pig, though, I think,
and I'd like to reach out to --

00:07:00.719 --> 00:07:02.221
again, we've established

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.723
a lot of those
in the farming community,

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:05.224
farm enthusiasts watch the show.

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:07.693
I think because of
a cloven hoof,

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:10.396
a pig could hold a cigarette.

00:07:10.396 --> 00:07:12.064
And we'll find out how
they smoke, but I would love --

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:13.899
I think we'll do a lot more pigs
smoking on the show

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:15.201
if this is...

00:07:15.201 --> 00:07:17.270
[ Inhales ]

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.105
Oink.

00:07:21.573 --> 00:07:24.577
Did a Larry David
yesterday that...

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:27.447
I think in retrospect
was pretty...

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:31.416
...pretty bad.

00:07:31.416 --> 00:07:33.452
Not gonna do it again,

00:07:33.452 --> 00:07:35.588
and just gonna
get ahead of it --

00:07:35.588 --> 00:07:37.956
same thing
with tonight's Brokaw,

00:07:37.956 --> 00:07:40.092
which you're seeing this
on Friday.

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:43.429
But on Thursday night,
thought I had a Brokaw.

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:45.598
Got away from me.

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:47.967
So before you even say it,
I hear you.

00:07:50.268 --> 00:07:51.437
Sang a couple lyrics from

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:53.939
Randy Newman's classic
"I Love L.A."

00:07:53.939 --> 00:07:56.976
I said, "I love L.A.,
I love it."

00:07:56.976 --> 00:07:58.277
Shame on me.

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:01.581
It's, "I love L.A., we love it."

00:08:02.881 --> 00:08:05.217
And that is a very important
song for me,

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:07.219
and this is a very true story.

00:08:07.219 --> 00:08:10.756
I moved to Los Angeles in 1999.

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:12.891
My brother and I moved there,
and our car --

00:08:12.891 --> 00:08:14.894
we went to Rent-a-Wreck,

00:08:14.894 --> 00:08:17.696
where we rented
a Ford Festiva for,

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:21.200
I think, like $400
the whole month,

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.734
which is a pretty good deal.

00:08:22.734 --> 00:08:26.606
A Ford Festiva is a very --
it's like a box.

00:08:27.572 --> 00:08:28.941
There's not much
to a Ford Festiva.

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:31.577
No one at a car dealership
has ever said,

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:33.446
"If you want
a little bit more..."

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:37.416
"...I'd love to show you
the Ford Festiva."

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.251
It had "Festiva" written --

00:08:39.251 --> 00:08:40.586
That's how I remember.

00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:43.088
"Festiva" was written in cursive
on the side.

00:08:43.088 --> 00:08:45.057
It was popular in an era
where people wanted

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:47.759
to see the name of their car
on the side of it,

00:08:47.759 --> 00:08:49.261
and we had a Ford Festiva.

00:08:49.261 --> 00:08:51.229
And I remember when we got it,
the guy said,

00:08:51.229 --> 00:08:53.766
"The only thing you should know

00:08:53.766 --> 00:08:56.068
is that the windshield wipers
don't work,"

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:57.402
and, you know,
coming from the East Coast,

00:08:57.402 --> 00:08:58.403
my brother and I said,

00:08:58.403 --> 00:08:59.438
"That seems like
a huge problem."

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:01.039
And he said,
"It never rains in L.A.,"

00:09:01.039 --> 00:09:02.508
and we were like, "Okay, cool."

00:09:02.508 --> 00:09:03.876
So we take the Ford Festiva,

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:08.047
and I remember
we stopped at a Tower Records

00:09:08.047 --> 00:09:11.216
and we bought Randy Newman's
greatest hits on cassette tape

00:09:11.216 --> 00:09:12.417
because we thought
it'd be super funny

00:09:12.417 --> 00:09:13.719
to drive around
in a Ford Festiva

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:17.689
our first week in L.A. blasting
"I Love L.A."

00:09:17.689 --> 00:09:20.025
in the worst car
that money could buy.

00:09:20.025 --> 00:09:22.861
And like our first night there,
it poured rain,

00:09:22.861 --> 00:09:24.263
and because we didn't have
windshield wipers,

00:09:24.263 --> 00:09:25.898
we had to pull over
on the side of the road

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:27.933
and just wait
for the rain to stop.

00:09:27.933 --> 00:09:29.735
And there was nothing
more depressing

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:32.905
than being, like,
new, young actors in L.A.

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:35.507
sitting on the side of the road
while you're hearing,

00:09:35.507 --> 00:09:36.909
like, Randy Newman be like

00:09:36.909 --> 00:09:43.783
[As Randy Newman] "From the
West Side to the East Side."

00:09:47.953 --> 00:09:50.756
We talked about the snap,

00:09:50.756 --> 00:09:53.291
the Thanos snap,
and we showed Wally --

00:09:53.291 --> 00:09:55.427
a wonderful work
by our graphics department.

00:09:55.427 --> 00:09:56.595
I know I give
the graphics department

00:09:56.595 --> 00:09:58.764
a bit of trouble here.

00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:02.268
Wonderful job by them of showing
Wally disintegrating,

00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:04.703
but then people said, "You know,
the problem with that graphic,

00:10:04.703 --> 00:10:06.772
which was great,
is that Wally's cue card

00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:08.107
would not have disintegrated.

00:10:08.107 --> 00:10:09.474
Wally would have disintegrated

00:10:09.474 --> 00:10:11.043
and the cue card would
have dropped to the ground,"

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:15.781
which is true if the cue card
wasn't a part of Wally.

00:10:15.781 --> 00:10:17.316
[ Laughter ]

00:10:17.316 --> 00:10:23.155
Wally's cue cards are to him
what our arms and legs are.

00:10:23.155 --> 00:10:24.990
It's been a part of him
since he was born.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.993
When when Wally was born...

00:10:29.628 --> 00:10:31.797
When Wally was born,
the doctor said,

00:10:31.797 --> 00:10:37.102
"It's a boy," not because...
he saw anything on Wally.

00:10:37.102 --> 00:10:38.637
He -- And thank you
for lending this to me, Wally,

00:10:38.637 --> 00:10:40.572
because I guess
your mom saved it.

00:10:40.572 --> 00:10:44.143
He said, "It's a boy," because
Wally was holding this.

00:10:44.143 --> 00:10:46.144
A tiny...

00:10:46.144 --> 00:10:47.680
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:54.319 --> 00:10:58.624
Heard from
the knitting community again.

00:10:58.624 --> 00:11:00.259
Same lovely woman.

00:11:03.095 --> 00:11:05.765
On Instagram, she like --
you know,

00:11:05.765 --> 00:11:07.566
we're living in an era right now

00:11:07.566 --> 00:11:09.267
where I think
everyone's, like, worried

00:11:09.267 --> 00:11:11.103
they did something 15 years ago

00:11:11.103 --> 00:11:13.138
that's gonna come back
to haunt them,

00:11:13.138 --> 00:11:18.744
and I did a photoshoot
years ago.

00:11:18.744 --> 00:11:21.113
And she just posted this photo,
and I'm paraphrasing.

00:11:21.113 --> 00:11:22.615
She was like, "The [bleep]"

00:11:22.615 --> 00:11:25.283
[ Laughter ]

00:11:25.283 --> 00:11:27.753
Because I guess -- if we could
go tight on the hands,

00:11:27.753 --> 00:11:30.790
I guess that's, like,
there's nothing about that

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.958
which is proper
knitting technique,

00:11:32.958 --> 00:11:35.961
and I'm so mad because
I remember doing that shoot,

00:11:35.961 --> 00:11:37.596
and they're like, "Maybe you
could be knitting a blanket."

00:11:37.596 --> 00:11:41.132
I'm like, "Guys,
I don't know how it works."

00:11:41.132 --> 00:11:43.134
And they're like, "Just do it.
What's gonna happen?"

00:11:43.134 --> 00:11:46.939
And I'm like, "I would just hate
to offend those...

00:11:46.939 --> 00:11:48.808
who, you know,
honor this craft,"

00:11:48.808 --> 00:11:51.476
and they're like,
"Don't worry about the knitters.

00:11:51.476 --> 00:11:53.111
What are they gonna do?
Hunt you down?"

00:11:53.111 --> 00:11:55.147
Well, they did.

00:11:55.147 --> 00:11:57.650
They did,
and as we've established,

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:03.122
they are foul-mouthed,
humorless.

00:12:03.122 --> 00:12:05.957
My Twitter feed is a cesspool...

00:12:05.957 --> 00:12:10.262
because of this at the time,
fun photo to take.

00:12:10.262 --> 00:12:11.997
What else we got?

00:12:15.267 --> 00:12:17.002
Okay.

00:12:19.271 --> 00:12:22.108
GoldenEye -- I talked about
the GoldenEye cheat codes,

00:12:22.108 --> 00:12:25.010
and I guess
a lot of people said...

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:26.445
I left out an "L."

00:12:26.445 --> 00:12:29.949
I left out a solitary "L."

00:12:29.949 --> 00:12:33.619
More than made up for by all
the L's who pointed that out.

00:12:35.087 --> 00:12:40.826
Had some "L" trouble
in general this week.

00:12:40.826 --> 00:12:44.530
We had a joke about Doritos,
cauliflower Doritos.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.631
Can we throw it up real quick,
Alex?

00:12:46.631 --> 00:12:51.103
You might be noticing...
"cauiflower."

00:12:51.103 --> 00:12:52.638
Cauiflower.

00:12:52.638 --> 00:12:54.973
You know, how the kids say it.

00:12:54.973 --> 00:12:56.642
Doritos is like,
"We'll do it a cool way.

00:12:56.642 --> 00:12:58.710
Cauiflower.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.279
Broli."

00:13:03.381 --> 00:13:07.419
"Me and my friends are going out
for some broli. Cauiflower."

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:11.957
Not the worst thing
graphics did to me this week.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:16.762
Alright, so I busted pretty hard

00:13:16.762 --> 00:13:18.197
on the graphics department
yesterday

00:13:18.197 --> 00:13:19.864
'cause we were
talking about LAX,

00:13:19.864 --> 00:13:20.933
and I was talking about
one time,

00:13:20.933 --> 00:13:23.268
I looked over in traffic,
was so bad at LAX

00:13:23.268 --> 00:13:26.272
that the car next to me
had a skeleton driving it.

00:13:26.272 --> 00:13:30.442
And the car was not
what I expected it to be.

00:13:30.442 --> 00:13:32.244
It was like an old...

00:13:32.244 --> 00:13:35.814
Volvo station wagon, basically,
and I gave it a lot of --

00:13:35.814 --> 00:13:37.116
can we show it real quick?

00:13:37.116 --> 00:13:38.617
Okay, so that's -- alright.

00:13:38.617 --> 00:13:39.985
Take it down, because I want
to say something.

00:13:39.985 --> 00:13:42.487
I went after graphics hard,
okay?

00:13:42.487 --> 00:13:44.289
And then I walk offstage,

00:13:44.289 --> 00:13:46.291
and Sal,
who writes "A Closer Look"

00:13:46.291 --> 00:13:49.761
and who is an honorable man,
said,

00:13:49.761 --> 00:13:50.929
"This is on me.

00:13:50.929 --> 00:13:52.964
They said, 'What kind of car?'

00:13:52.964 --> 00:13:56.335
And I said,
'Like an old Volvo.'"

00:13:56.335 --> 00:13:59.471
Now, obviously,
Sal is no longer with the show.

00:13:59.471 --> 00:14:02.508
[ Laughter ]

00:14:05.577 --> 00:14:10.916
But I felt bad,
and I was gonna go down...

00:14:10.916 --> 00:14:14.286
down to where graphics are.

00:14:14.286 --> 00:14:17.088
You know, we're right now --
we're on the eighth floor.

00:14:17.088 --> 00:14:20.759
Graphics is, what, negative 50?

00:14:20.759 --> 00:14:23.162
You have to take
three elevators down.

00:14:26.598 --> 00:14:28.934
They're, like, buried deep
in a part of the building

00:14:28.934 --> 00:14:31.103
that you kind of
can't believe exists,

00:14:31.103 --> 00:14:32.637
and I was gonna go down there
to apologize to them

00:14:32.637 --> 00:14:33.939
because I felt so bad.

00:14:33.939 --> 00:14:35.941
But then, you know,
I read some of the comments,

00:14:35.941 --> 00:14:39.411
and people said, "Hey,
the car is not the problem.

00:14:39.411 --> 00:14:43.281
The problem is you described
a car stuck in traffic

00:14:43.281 --> 00:14:46.618
at LAX, and they gave you a car

00:14:46.618 --> 00:14:50.956
that was speeding ahead
on open road!"

00:14:50.956 --> 00:14:54.159
Let's take another look.

00:14:54.159 --> 00:14:55.393
It's blurry.

00:14:55.393 --> 00:14:57.596
The background is blurry,

00:14:57.596 --> 00:14:59.631
that skeleton
is driving so fast,

00:14:59.631 --> 00:15:01.900
so you know what?

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.969
You're going the way
of Sal, everybody.

00:15:09.074 --> 00:15:14.612
Lastly, we were
very happy to announce...

00:15:14.612 --> 00:15:17.750
we finished second for the Emmy,
tied for second.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.752
[ Laughter ]

00:15:20.752 --> 00:15:22.921
Very nice for the Emmy,
the Academy to reach out

00:15:22.921 --> 00:15:26.224
and say, "Tied for second,
four-way tie."

00:15:26.224 --> 00:15:27.559
Which is great, second.

00:15:27.559 --> 00:15:30.262
We lost to "Carpool Karaoke,"
which I've said before

00:15:30.262 --> 00:15:34.933
is maybe one of the greatest
talk-show bits of all time

00:15:34.933 --> 00:15:37.936
and a very deserving winner
of the Emmy.

00:15:37.936 --> 00:15:40.772
Like, it's so good
that I feel like...

00:15:40.772 --> 00:15:42.774
I almost want to, like,
change the name of this

00:15:42.774 --> 00:15:44.242
to, like, sound more like it,

00:15:44.242 --> 00:15:47.413
if there was anything
that made sense at all.

00:15:47.413 --> 00:15:49.948
But I don't think there is,

00:15:49.948 --> 00:15:54.786
and I also think that
at the end, it's not about...

00:15:54.786 --> 00:15:56.455
winning or losing.

00:15:56.455 --> 00:16:02.428
It's about the jackals you tried
to avoid meeting along the way.

00:16:03.729 --> 00:16:05.731
But I didn't avoid it.
I met you all.

00:16:05.731 --> 00:16:09.101
And if I had won, it was
going to be mine and mine alone,

00:16:09.101 --> 00:16:11.403
but I do feel like
we lost together.

00:16:11.403 --> 00:16:15.274
[ Laughter ]

00:16:15.274 --> 00:16:16.642
Also, people said,

00:16:16.642 --> 00:16:18.410
"Hey, do you feel bad that
you, like, really pushed it?

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:21.246
You had a lot of, like,
'for your consideration' stuff,

00:16:21.246 --> 00:16:22.914
a lot of, like, FYC stuff."

00:16:22.914 --> 00:16:25.417
I want to clarify, a lot
of people said this was an FYC.

00:16:25.417 --> 00:16:28.754
This is a Fine Young Cannibals
mug, okay?

00:16:28.754 --> 00:16:31.256
[ Laughter ]

00:16:31.256 --> 00:16:34.960
This has nothing to do with...
an award push.

00:16:36.295 --> 00:16:40.599
So again, congratulations to
everybody at "Carpool Karaoke,"

00:16:40.599 --> 00:16:44.603
and congratulations
to the other nominees.

00:16:44.603 --> 00:16:48.273
And it's been lovely
having you see me,

00:16:48.273 --> 00:16:51.276
and I look forward to
you seeing me again next week.

00:16:51.276 --> 00:16:55.614
And in all sincerity,
this is -- all jokes aside,

00:16:55.614 --> 00:16:57.949
this is my favorite part
of the week.

00:16:57.949 --> 00:17:02.487
Thank you so much for watching,
and we'll see you.

00:17:02.487 --> 00:17:04.556
Well, I don't know.
However you want me to say it.

00:17:04.556 --> 00:17:08.193
You guys record yourself
saying it and play it at the end

00:17:08.193 --> 00:17:09.861
so that it's satisfying
to your ears.

00:17:09.861 --> 00:17:11.596
Each one of you different
because you know what?

00:17:11.596 --> 00:17:15.233
Jackals are like snowflakes.
You're all different.

00:17:15.233 --> 00:17:18.103
And you're also like
the modern use of "snowflakes,"

00:17:18.103 --> 00:17:20.572
which is you're [bleep]
irritated by everything.

00:17:20.572 --> 00:17:23.609
[ Laughter ]

